Applying the chain rule in the $y$ coordinates, $W'_m
 =\frac{\partial S}{\partial y^m}
 =\frac{\partial x^p}{\partial y^m}
  \frac{\partial S}{\partial x^p}
 =\frac{\partial x^p}{\partial y^m}\,W_p.$ This is the transformation law of a covariant vector, or covector. The Jacobian is the inverse of the one in [eq:contravariant-vector]; lower and upper indices therefore encode different transformation behavior.

